<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87730" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκατα-τίθημι</span></b> , in aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκατέθηκεν,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθηκεν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> mostly 
				Med.
			, <i>set down before,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν λόγον</span>
			<i>make an introductory</i> statement, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lay up in store,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάριν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					19.1.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεργεσίαν ἔς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					48.30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
